## DESCRIPTION
## Use a basis of sines and cosines, find the matrix representing the derivative.
## ENDDESCRIPTION


## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Linear transformations)
## DBsection(Associated matrices)
## Date(September 5, 2008)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Peter Staab)
## KEYWORDS('basis', 'sines', 'cosines')

# updated 2022.12.12

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.
loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "PGcourse.pl",);

Context("Vector");

($k, $j) = random_subset(2, 1 .. 4);

$f1 = Formula("sin($k x)")->reduce;
$f2 = Formula("cos($k x)")->reduce;
$f3 = Formula("sin($j x)")->reduce;
$f4 = Formula("cos($j x)")->reduce;

$ans = Matrix([
    [ 0, -$k, 0, 0 ], [ $k, 0, 0, 0 ], [ 0, 0, 0, -$j ], [ 0, 0, $j, 0 ] ]);

BEGIN_PGML
Consider the subspace, [`V`] of all continuous functions where
[` V =  \{ a\, [$f1] + b\,[$f2] + c\,[$f3] + d\, [$f4] \; |\; a,b,c,d \in \mathbb{R} \} `]
Let the linear map [` D: V \rightarrow V `] be the derivative.
Find the matrix that represents the map in the standard basis
[` B = ([$f1], [$f2], [$f3], [$f4]) `]

Hint: for each basis element, find the derivative and write the derivative in terms of [`B`].  The columns of the resulting matrix are these representations.

[___]*{$ans}

END_PGML

$arg1 = Formula("$k x")->reduce;
$arg2 = Formula("$j x")->reduce;
$f1   = Formula("$k cos($arg1)")->reduce;
$f2   = Formula("-$k sin($arg1)")->reduce;
$f3   = Formula("$j cos($arg2)")->reduce;
$f4   = Formula("$j sin($arg2)")->reduce;

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
In this case, recall that 
[``` \begin{aligned}
\frac{d}{x} \sin ([$arg1]) & = [$f1] \\
\frac{d}{x} \cos ([$arg1]) & = [$f2] \\
\frac{d}{x} \sin ([$arg2]) & = [$f3] \\
\frac{d}{x} \cos ([$arg2]) & = [$f4]
\end{aligned}
```]
The four output functions are writen in terms of the basis.  For example [`[$f1] `]
can be written as 
[``` \begin{bmatrix} 0 \\ [$k] \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{bmatrix} ```]
and continuing this for the other three output functions, then written as vectors,
the output matrix is
[``` [$ans] ```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();    # This should be the last executable line in the problem.
